  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Cook rice: Rinse the rice until the water runs clear. Put in a small saucepan with 310ml (1¼ cups) water, cover and bring to a simmer over medium heat. Reduce the heat to low and cook for 13 mins or until tender and the water is absorbed. Turn off the heat and stand, covered, for at least 5 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/448846/photos/large/71778_1-39eb2ebbacec1875cab6a8219f5bfd51.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Meanwhile, thinly slice the capsicum. Trim the broccolini and halve lengthwise. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Combine the sweet chilli sauce (see Make it yours), 1 tbs tomato sauce, 1 tbs soy sauce, 1 tsp white vinegar and 1 tbs water in a bowl.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/448850/photos/large/71778_2-685ada51c836c7e2159a8d8219ac8bfd.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook chicken-style strips: Heat 1 tbs vegetable oil in a medium deep frypan over medium-high heat. Stir-fry the chicken-style strips for 3-4 mins until browned and warmed through. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/448852/photos/large/71778_3-613c21184ef0ccccc3a9bc3f43e9319e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook veggies: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in the same pan over high heat. Add the capsicum, broccolini, garlic and 2 tsp water and cook, covered, for 2-3 mins until tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/448853/photos/large/71778_4-e7f07c2317b92a49e86617eeb6ec5e9f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the chicken-style strips and sauce mixture to the veggies and stir-fry for 30 secs or until warmed through. Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the rice and stir-fry among bowls, scatter over the peanuts and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/448855/photos/large/71778_5-f0ec67c1816620694963f67e3b7a46b0.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: The sweet chilli sauce has a mild kick. If you want to reduce the heat, substitute with a little more tomato sauce.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/448856/photos/large/71778_6-ed14f7fefd49e2380614b5c7023dafa8.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
